course: dictionary
lesson: 11601
title: A part that sticks out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An appendage is a part that sticks out from the main body of a creature or thing, such as an arm, leg, tail, antenna or fin. «The crab waved one of its large claws at us.» The claw is an appendage, because it sticks out from the crab's body.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. An appendage can be something added to a bigger, more important thing. «The new garden shed is an appendage to our house.» The shed is joined on to the house, but the house is the main thing.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence is about animals, insects or body parts, it means a part that sticks out. If the sentence is about something added on to a bigger thing, it means the second meaning. Ask yourself: is this a part of a body, or something joined onto a main thing?
fact: Appendage is a noun, and its plural is appendages.
fact: An appendage is a part that sticks out from the main body.
fact: Arms, legs, tails, antennae and fins are all examples of appendages.
fact: «Appendage» can also mean something added to a bigger, more important thing.
fact: Crabs and lobsters use their appendages to walk, grip and feel things.
exercise: Which of these is an appendage? | A cloud | *A fin on a fish | A tail | A cup
exercise: «The extra room was an appendage to the old house.» What does appendage mean here? | A small pet | A broken window | *Something added to a bigger, more important thing | A part that sticks out from an animal
exercise: «The lobster used its appendages to grip the rock.» What are the appendages in this sentence? | The sun shining on the water | The rock | The sea | *Its claws and legs
test: «The crab lost one appendage in a fight, but it grew another.» What is an appendage in this sentence? | The fight | Its shell | *A claw or leg that sticks out from the crab's body | A rock pool
test: Which sentence uses appendage to mean something added to a bigger thing? | «The fish swam fast past the rock.» | «The octopus waved its long appendages.» | *«The new shed is an appendage to our house.» | «The bell rang at noon.»
exam: Which word fits? A ___ is a part that sticks out from the main body, like a tail or a fin. | dictionary | *appendage | ladder | pebble
